  "articleBody": "Basement remodels are a great way to add value and space to your home, but it's easy to stumble if you're not careful. Let's talk about some common pitfalls and how to steer clear of them. First off, a big mistake is starting without checking for moisture problems. You absolutely need to address any water issues or leaks before you even think about framing or drywall. Ignoring local egress or headroom requirements is another common oversight; these aren't just suggestions, they're critical for safety and code compliance. We've also seen folks hire contractors based solely on the lowest price without checking credentials, insurance, or references. That can lead to a lot of frustration. Another common error is not planning for utility placement, like plumbing and electrical, before the walls go up. And finally, some homeowners forget about dust control during the project. It's important to keep those channels of communication open with your contractor throughout the entire process. By avoiding these common mistakes, you can help ensure your basement remodel goes smoothly and delivers the results you're hoping for. When your project involves complex elements like waterproofing or major electrical work, bringing in an experienced pro is definitely the way to go.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
